.TH "listSequences" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
listSequences \- Enumerate sequences information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.listSequences()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to enumerate the sequence information of the current
database.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return a detailed list of
collections through the cursor.Users can refer to $LIST_SEQUENCES to get the
returned field information.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When exception happens, use getLastError() to get the error code and use
getLastErrMsg() to get error message.
For more details, please reference to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v3.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
\f[C]"Name":\ "SYS_8589934593_id_SEQ"\ }\f[]
